# broker#21 - installed as /etc/default/earlyoom.
#
# A shedder of the node's small daemons, NOT a killer of dev tooling (broker#58).
# VSCode Server, Claude Code and SocratiCode inherit exe.dev's oom_score_adj
# -1000, which earlyoom 1.7 skips outright, as the kernel does: nothing on this
# node can kill them. What it can reach is any process above -1000 whose
# oom_score stays above 0 after --avoid - small daemons: the session
# dbus-daemon, (sd-pam), cron, polkitd, logind, timesyncd, and journald, which
# is at adj -250 and still scores 202 - tens of MiB in all, journald's evidence
# included. So it is INSTALLED AND DISABLED (broker#58); this file is kept
# current for the day sessions stop being exempt, when
# `systemctl enable --now earlyoom` is the whole change.
#
#   -r 3600   one memory report an hour in the journal (the package default)
#   -m 10     SIGTERM below 10% available (~790 MiB at 8 GB), SIGKILL below 5%.
#             There is no swap, so earlyoom's swap condition always holds and
#             memory alone decides.
#   --avoid   the bus and the way in: redis-server, tailscaled, systemd*,
#             dbus-daemon, and exe.dev's own exe-init and sshd. Only -300, not
#             an exclusion: the drop-ins' OOMScoreAdjust=-900 is what takes the
#             bus's oom_score under 300, so --avoid lands it below earlyoom's
#             badness-0 starting victim, which it never replaces with less
#   --prefer  dev tooling: node, npx (titled `npm exec <pkg>`), and VSCode
#             Server's node processes, whose comm is MainThread. Inert while
#             sessions sit at -1000 - a dry run prints them at 300, the score
#             before the skip; read its `new victim` lines, not that column
#
# No -p: it needs CAP_SYS_NICE, which this DynamicUser unit does not have.
#
# Regexes are space-free and carry NO BACKSLASH. The unit runs
# `earlyoom $EARLYOOM_ARGS`, and systemd splits that on whitespace, strips
# quotes, and drops a backslash for the character after it: `\.` would reach
# earlyoom as `.`, matching anything. tests/deploy/test_memory_protection.py
# pins both lists and the host class they assume.
EARLYOOM_ARGS="-r 3600 -m 10 --avoid ^(redis-server|tailscaled|systemd.*|dbus-daemon|exe-init|sshd)$ --prefer ^(node|npm.*|npx|MainThread)$"
